# Branch Names

Use conventional branch names: `type/short-description`.

## Format

```
type/short-description
```

- **type:** same vocabulary as commits — `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `perf`, `style`, `build`, `revert`
- **description:** kebab-case, brief, imperative or noun phrase
- No issue IDs, usernames, or ticket prefixes in the branch name unless the user asks for them

## Examples

```text
feat/skill-loader
fix/reject-non-skill-paths
chore/bootstrap-hooks
ci/github-actions
docs/readme-ci-section
```

```text
# ❌ Linear-style or username prefixes
danielwaltersdev/dan-6-set-up-github-ci
# ❌ spaces, underscores, or missing type
feat_skill_loader
skill-loader
```

When creating a branch for work in this repo, follow this format unless the user specifies a different name.
